  "notes": "From the garden views: a two-storey house of pale painted brick facing a long lawn and, across it, a pool. The ground floor is a deep gallery under the upper storey's parapet band, glazed at the back, with a corner pier, one middle pier and a barbecue bay with a grill in its back wall, dark timber soffit; above, a planted terrace (dark planters of feather grass along the edge) in front of the set-back upper storey with its thin concrete eave and a tall brick band on top; two black flues at the terrace's end; a brick chimney fin on the west end. The side entrance (louvred aluminium canopy, concrete canopy over stepped brick volumes) is placed on the east end. The street side, the plan depth and window positions on the north and ends are guessed. Painted brick drawn as render; the grasses as thatch."
